<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-ALPHAND WINS VAL GARDENA DOWNHILL.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-ALPHAND WINS VAL GARDENA DOWNHILL.</headline>
<dateline>VAL GARDENA, Italy 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Luc Alphand won a shortened men's Alpine skiing World Cup downhill on Friday in an unofficial time of one minute 53.10 seconds.</p>
<p>Norway's Atle Skaardal was second in 1:53.25 and Italian Kristian Ghedina was third in 1:53.30, also according to provisional results.</p>
</text>
